The Dirty Pipe Linux kernel vulnerability (CVE-2021-35947) is a type of LPE (Local Privilege Escalation) that affects Linux kernels. It allows a user to write data to a pipe and then read it back, potentially leading to privilege escalation. The vulnerability is related to the way the Linux kernel handles pipes and can be exploited to write data to a pipe and then read it back, leading to a race condition.

